      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary issue is the inherent conflict between the UN's universal principles and the absolute right of sovereign states to self-govern. Powerful member states often prioritize their own geopolitical or economic interests, leading to partisan block voting that supersedes impartial action. Furthermore, the UN often lacks strong, independent enforcement power, making it reliant on the political will of its most powerful and self-interested members to act decisively.",
